        "answer": {
          "short": "Ignore every occurrence of the digits 3, 6 and 9: each contributes a multiple of 3 to the digit sum. The remaining digits are 8, 2, 2, 1 and 5, whose sum is 18.",
          "worked": "Every occurrence of 3, 6 or 9 contributes a multiple of 3 to the digit sum, so these digits can be ignored. The five remaining digits give\n\n$$\\begin{align*}8+2+2+1+5&=18.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince 18 is divisible by 3, the original number is divisible by 3.",
